.TH "QBITTORRENT" "1" "August 2026" "Bittorrent client written in C++ / Qt"
.SH NAME
qBittorrent \- a Bittorrent client written in C++ / Qt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]qbittorrent\f[R] \f[CR][options] [(<filename> | <url>)...]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]qbittorrent\f[R] \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]qbittorrent\f[R] \f[CR]\-\-version\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]qBittorrent\f[R] is an advanced Bittorrent client written in C++ /
Qt, using the \f[B]libtorrent\-rasterbar\f[R] library by Arvid Norberg.
qBittorrent is similar to uTorrent.
qBittorrent is fast, stable, light, it supports unicode and it provides
a good integrated search engine.
It also comes with UPnP port forwarding / NAT\-PMP, encryption (Vuze
compatible), FAST extension (mainline) and PeX support (utorrent
compatible).
.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]\f[CB]\-h | \-\-help\f[B]\f[R] Display this help message and exit.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-v | \-\-version\f[B]\f[R] Display program version and exit.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-confirm\-legal\-notice\f[B]\f[R] Confirm the legal
notice.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-webui\-port=<port>\f[B]\f[R] Change the WebUI port.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-torrenting\-port=<port>\f[B]\f[R] Change the torrenting
port.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-no\-splash\f[B]\f[R] Disable splash screen.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-profile=<dir>\f[B]\f[R] Store configuration files in
\f[CR]<dir>\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-configuration=<name>\f[B]\f[R] Store configuration files
in directories qBittorrent_\f[CR]<name>\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-relative\-fastresume\f[B]\f[R] Hack into libtorrent
fastresume files and make file paths relative to the profile directory.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB](<filename> | <url>)...\f[B]\f[R] Download the torrents
passed by the user.
.SS Options when adding new torrents
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-save\-path=<path>\f[B]\f[R] Torrent save path.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-add\-stopped=<true|false>\f[B]\f[R] Add torrents as
running or stopped.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-seed\-mode\f[B]\f[R] Seed mode.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-category=<name>\f[B]\f[R] Assign torrents to category.
If the category doesn\(cqt exist, it will be created.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-sequential\f[B]\f[R] Download files in sequential order.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-first\-and\-last\f[B]\f[R] Download first and last pieces
first.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-skip\-dialog=<true|false>\f[B]\f[R] Specify whether the
\(lqAdd New Torrent\(rq dialog opens when adding a torrent.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Option values may be supplied via environment variables.
For an option named `parameter\-name', the environment variable name is
`QBT_PARAMETER_NAME' (upper case, with `\-' replaced by \(cq_`).
To pass flag values, set the variable to \(cq1' or `TRUE'.
For example, to disable the splash screen:
.IP
.EX
